  "description": "Reid Vantage 1 | Endurance road bike\nLightweight, comfortable and built for longer rides – a versatile endurance road bike for fitness cycling, road adventures and exploring beyond the tarmac.\nThe Reid Bikes Vantage 1 combines a lightweight aluminium frame, full carbon fibre fork and reliable Shimano components to deliver an excellent balance of performance, comfort and value. Designed for riders looking to develop their road cycling, tackle longer distances or explore new routes, it's a capable all-rounder for everyday and recreational riding.\nIts double-butted hydroformed aluminium frame provides a responsive yet lightweight foundation, with a tapered head tube and internal cable routing for a clean finish. The full carbon fibre fork helps reduce weight and absorb road vibrations, while endurance-focused geometry and specially designed ovalised seatstays provide additional comfort over longer distances.\nA Shimano Claris 16-speed drivetrain offers reliable gear changes and a versatile range for tackling climbs and maintaining momentum on flatter roads. The compact 50/34T Prowheel chainset is paired with an 11-32T Shimano cassette, providing practical gearing for varied routes. Shimano Claris integrated shifters combine braking and gear controls for convenient operation.\nTektro C310 mechanical disc brakes with 160mm rotors deliver dependable stopping power and control in changing weather conditions. The Vantage 1 also features 700c double-wall alloy wheels fitted with Kenda Kriterium 700x30mm tyres, offering a balance of rolling efficiency, grip and comfort across different road surfaces.\nFinished with compact alloy drop handlebars, comfortable bar tape and a sport saddle, the Reid Bikes Vantage 1 is designed to make longer rides more enjoyable. Combining quality components, lightweight construction and endurance-focused comfort, it's a versatile road bike for riders looking to go further.\nThe Reid Bikes Vantage 1 is ideal for:\n\nEndurance road cycling, with comfortable geometry for longer days in the saddle\n\nFitness and recreational riding, with a lightweight frame and responsive handling\n\nLong-distance adventures, with a carbon fibre fork and comfort-focused frame design\n\nTackling hills and varied routes, with Shimano Claris 16-speed gearing and a compact chainset\n\nReliable all-weather braking, with Tektro mechanical disc brakes and 160mm rotors\n\nRoad comfort and control, with Kenda 700x30mm tyres and a full carbon fibre fork\n\nRiders progressing their road cycling, with quality Shimano components and versatile performance\n\nExploring different road surfaces, with wider-volume tyres suited to paved roads and harder-packed routes",
